    exampleHands: [
      'Setup example: 6 card(s) per player.',
      'Rule example: Win a hand by being first to play enough distance cards to reach the target (1000 km in 4- or 6-player team play; 700 km in 2- or 3-player with option to extend to 1000). Win the game by being first to reach 5000 cumulative points.',
      'Turn-flow example: On your turn draw one card, then play one card or discard. Play Roll to drive; play distance cards (25–200 km) when Roll is showing; max two 200 km per hand. Play hazards on opponents; play remedies on your battle/speed area; play safeties for immunity and optional coup-fourré. Discard when no legal play. Hand ends when someone reaches target distance or all cards are played.',
      'Scoring example: Points per hand: 1 per km traveled; 100 per safety; 300 bonus for all four safeties; 300 per coup-fourré; 400 for completing the trip; 300 delayed action (trip after stock exhausted); 300 safe trip (no 200 km cards); 200 extension bonus; 500 shutout (opponent played no distance). Game ends when one side reaches 5000 points; if both exceed 5000 in the same hand, higher total wins. First to reach 5000 cumulative points. Each hand won by first to reach target distance (1000 km or 700 km in 2–3 player with optional extension)..',
